.TH PANTHER 1 "2026" "Panther" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
panther \- local network scanner and mapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B panther
[\fB\-\-lang\fR \fIfr\fR|\fIen\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
.br
.B panther \-\-cli
[\fB\-\-depth\fR \fIecoute\fR|\fIrapide\fR|\fInormal\fR|\fIapprofondi\fR] [\fB\-\-target\fR \fICIDR\fR]... [\fB\-\-iface\fR \fIIFACE\fR] [\fB\-\-security\fR]
.br
.B panther \-\-web
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Panther
discovers the devices of a local network (phones, printers, TVs, cameras, NAS, switches\&...), draws the map, tracks their presence
over time, handles several networks and VLANs, compares two scans and exports reports.
The scan engine is written in standard-library Python; only the graphical interface needs PyQt6.
.PP
Only use it on networks you are responsible for or have written permission to scan.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Scan and print a table in the terminal, without any interface.
.TP
.B \-\-web
Serve a local web interface (127.0.0.1 only) instead of opening the window.
.TP
.BI \-\-target " CIDR"
Extra range to scan (VLAN, routed subnet). May be repeated. Public ranges are refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " LEVEL"
Scan depth for \fB\-\-cli\fR: \fIecoute\fR (listen only: nothing is sent on the network), \fIrapide\fR, \fInormal\fR (default) or \fIapprofondi\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-iface " IFACE"
Network interface to scan (default: the interface of the default route).
.TP
.B \-\-security
Enable the read-only security analysis (open ports, banners, services reachable without a password). It never tries a credential.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Try the interface on a fictional network: nothing is scanned, no configuration is read or written.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " LANG"
Interface language, \fIfr\fR or \fIen\fR. Default: the saved choice, then the system's.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port of the web interface (default 8765).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Detailed log, also printed on the console.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/Panther/panther.db
History (devices, scans, events), readable by the owner only.
.TP
.I ~/.config/Panther/devices.json
Names and types set by hand.
.TP
.I ~/.config/Panther/rules.json
Custom detection rules (see /usr/share/doc/panther-netscan/RULES.md).
.TP
.I ~/.config/Panther/panther.log
Error log (device addresses and names, never a password).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lldpd (8),
.BR ip (8)
